FORMAT

Formats one partition of an additional data drive as FAT32.

Usage:
    format <drive-number> <partition-index> fat32 --yes

Drive and partition indexes are zero-based. For example, the first partition on Drive0 is selected as:
    format 0 0 fat32 --yes

If DRIVES reports partitions=0, create a partition table first, for example:
    partition 0 1
    format 0 0 fat32 --yes

Formatting destroys existing filesystem data on the selected partition. Mounted partitions are refused.
